			<div class="content" id="post-content-4690297">
									

<p>It's a YouTube channel with reality-altering properties. The article is kind of long (~2500 words)</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p>I got greenlights <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-13400363/this-channel-does-not-exist#">here</a>.</p>
<p>All the images I used are public domain and I can provide sources if needed.</p>
<p>The basic idea is a YouTube channel that erases things from existence by making videos about them. Mainly, I'm wondering if the containment procedures, a character's journal, and video transcripts are good. I also want to know if the story of the article flows and hangs together properly over all. Thank you for looking at my draft!</p>
<p><a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/cyborgoctopus">Sandbox page.</a></p>

