<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><em>Placeholder, will critique soon</em></span><br />
Hey there CyborgOctopus, I'm here for review of your draft! For some reason this really reminds me Don't Hug me I'm Scared. Definitely creepy vibes!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;The&nbsp;info&nbsp;you&nbsp;seek</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>All platforms for the dissemination of video content are to be monitored by Foundation observation software &quot;Panoptes&quot; for SCP-XXXX.</code>
</pre></div>
<br />
Personally such a task I feel is a bit too large for mere software to monitor it. I would think an AIC would be more plausible to monitor this as looking for specific videos across the internet would require complexity.
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>Upon alert by this software, SCP-XXXX must be removed as quickly as possible. In the event that removal is difficult, the affected platform must be disabled until it is complete.</code>
</pre></div>
<br />
I feel this could be phrased better. &quot;Once alerted, Foundation webcrawler X is to expunge/remove media in question. I feel as quickly as possible is a bit implied given the nature of the Foundation.
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>This may be the subject itself (if it is a single individual), a representative member of the subject (if a group of individuals), or have some otherwise significant relation.</code>
</pre></div>
<br />
How do we know this? There is nothing in the document(correct me if I missed it) that details what happens when multiple people at once witness it. I would perhaps include an example where such a thing occurs.
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>█████████,</code>
</pre></div>
<br />
Why is a Junior Researcher's name censored? Do we just not know it due to the effects of the SCP? As it stands, I can't see why it would be removed. The same can be said for the Site Director. All in all I would be careful with censoring, it should always add to the article its used in or make sense why something would be censored.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Overall&nbsp;Thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;The&nbsp;Final&nbsp;Thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Overall this seems to be free of SPaG errors, and the clinical tone for the document is appropriate. I would be careful on what you censor again, as it seems a lot has been removed with no real reason why it needed to be removed. Other than that, I like the added entries on examples of their videos, and how they may have potentially erased these things or at the very least memory of said things. With some minor edits, I think this would be a successful article and look forward to seeing it on the mainsite. I would also reach out to the people who gave you your greenlights and see what they think! Best of luck</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

