<p>Now there's a lot more information in the previous entry, so they both add some different aspects.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>So I do like the transition to the final log: he’s slowly losing his faculties and ability to write coherent sentences. What I’m not too sure of are the dreams of the “faceless things”. There’s no prior hints of the SCP being able to affect one’s dreams or memories, so this effect might be viewed as extraneous.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wanted to leave the dreams part kind of ambiguous. It could really just be a dream brought on by stress, or the production crew could be watching him and preparing to erase him.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Note that you tend to repeat information in the addenda titles and then in the foreword of the addenda again. I would revise the foreword to explain the context of each addendum a little more. For example, in Addendum 3, make it clear why the Foundation is studying these videos; why are they important?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hopefully I've made it more clear why the videos are important and what stands out about each one.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>So this was a nice touch to the ending: actually describing the video that triggered Hollister’s disappearance. What I’m unclear about is what he’s saying, and its implications: Why is SCP-xxxx “great admirers” of the Foundation? And what are its motives such that it wants to “collaborate” and make peace? They did just make one of their researchers disappear, so why is it suddenly peaceful?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Tried to improve this section so it's clear that whoever is behind SCP-XXXX admires the Foundation's (or possibly humanity/our universe's) &quot;performance&quot; and doesn't see anything wrong with what they're doing - they view it as peaceful and collaborative.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Another issue is the timeline of events: does this video appear first or does Hollister disappear first? You might want to indicate the posting date of each of these videos at the start of each transcript, just for clarity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Added a clarification to the notes section suggesting the video was posted at pretty much the same time Hollister disappeared.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
